{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And there was a famine in the land.</b> Yitzhak thought that the Egyptian exile was about to begin immediately. HaShem said to him: Do not go down to Egypt — meaning, the exile destined to be in Egypt does not begin now." "<b>Besides the first famine.</b> Scripture teaches you that this was the second one, and so Rav Yosef translated in Megillat Ruth." "<b>And Yitzhak went to Avimelekh.</b> Who was his father's ally." "<b>King of the Philistines, Gerar.</b> Yitzhak's intention was to go down to Egypt by way of the land of the Philistines, because it is close."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:59.847161471Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}